<title>SINGAPORE: CSA 1996 net profit up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>CSA 1996 net profit up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		    14.55   vs   13.22</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)		10.00   vs   10.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	   11.38   vs   10.35</p>
<p>    Turnover		     445.24   vs  372.57</p>
<p>    Investment income	    0.37   vs    0.34</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    36.09   vs   35.45</p>
<p>    Interest expense	     4.37   vs    3.94</p>
<p>    Depreciation		  13.95   vs   11.64</p>
<p>    Associates		     1.94   vs    0.74</p>
<p>    Tax				4.88   vs    4.36</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (0.28)  vs   (3.03)</p>
<p>    Extraordinary		  0.32   vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - CSA Holdings Ltd said performance is not expected to be maintained at the same level as in 1996. This is due to the reduced contribution from its wholly-owned subsidiary Computer Systems Advisors (M) Bhd (CSAM) as a result of its shareholding dilution to below 50 percent after the listing. CSA said the sale of its share will result in an extraordinary gain in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
